
# `include/` — firmware architecture + how to add apps

This firmware is built around a small menu/app framework (all in headers under `include/`) with a single `loop()` entrypoint in `src/main.cpp`.

## Key concepts

### Input

- `InputEvent` (`include/input_event.h`): `UP`, `DOWN`, `LEFT`, `RIGHT`, `CENTER`.
- `InputHandler` (`include/input_handler.h`): interface with `on_input(InputEvent)`.
- `InputDispatcher` (`include/input_dispatcher.h`): singleton that debounces GPIO and dispatches **only to the top** of a stack of `InputHandler*`.

Flow:

1. `loop()` calls `InputDispatcher::poll()`
2. `poll()` reads buttons and dispatches rising-edge events to `handlers.top()`

### Menu + apps

- `MenuNode` (`include/menu_node.h`): tree node with `name` and `children`.
- `App` (`include/app.h`): a `MenuNode` that is also an `InputHandler`, with:
  - `on_enter()`, `on_exit()`, `tick()`, `draw()`, `on_input()`
  - `exit()` helper that calls `on_exit()`, sets `wants_exit_`, and pops itself from the input stack.
- `MenuManager` (`include/menu_manager.h`): singleton `InputHandler` that:
  - navigates the `MenuNode` tree (UP/DOWN select, LEFT back)
  - on `CENTER`, enters an `App` by calling `app->on_enter()` and pushing it onto `InputDispatcher`
  - calls `tick()` on the active app; otherwise draws the menu.

### Display + UI helpers

- `Display` (`include/display.h`): primitive drawing wrapper (text/rects/clear).
- `ui` (`include/ui.h`): shared drawing + interaction helpers:
  - `draw_status(display, text)` for a one-line header
  - `draw_list(display, items, selected_index)` for the standard menu/list view
  - `draw_confirm(display, message)` for blocking confirm prompts
  - `apply_list_nav(event, selected_index, count)` to share UP/DOWN list navigation
  - `clamp_index(idx, count)` to keep selection in-bounds when list sizes change

## How to add a new app

1. Create a header in `include/apps/<your_app>.h`:
   - Derive from `flopper::App`
   - Implement: `on_enter`, `on_exit`, `tick`, `draw`, `on_input`
   - Use `exit()` on LEFT/back (or when you want to return to the menu)
   - For list UIs, prefer:
     - `ui::apply_list_nav(e, selected_, items_count)` in `on_input`
     - `ui::draw_status(...)` + `ui::draw_list(...)` in `draw()`

2. Register it in the menu tree (`include/menu_tree.h`):
   - `#include "apps/<your_app>.h"`
   - Add an `inline <YourApp> your_app;`
   - Add it to a menu in `build_menu_tree()` via `some_menu.add_child(&your_app);`

3. Rebuild/flash as usual (see repo root `README.md` for PlatformIO setup).

## Notes / patterns

- `MenuNode` and all `App` instances in `menu_tree.h` are `inline` globals; the tree is rebuilt at boot via `build_menu_tree()`.
- `MenuManager` should stay on the dispatcher stack under an app; it will resume drawing the menu after an app exits.
- For dynamic lists whose size can change between frames, always clamp the selected index when drawing.
